## Project Architecture for Save/Load System — Full Findings

I thoroughly explored the pneumatic-circuit simulation Unity project (Hypertonic.GridPlacement + custom Valve/Bezier systems). All core classes located and read. There is **NO existing save/load or serialization system for runtime valve/wire state** — one must be built from scratch. Below is the complete architecture.

### 1. Component Placement (GridManager / GridPlacement / Item3D)
- **Spawn flow** (`Assets\Scripts\CreateItemBtn.cs` and `Assets\Scripts\UI_TestPanelItemBTN.cs`): instantiate prefab → enter grid placement mode → register in scene list:
  ```csharp
  objectToPlace = Instantiate(_gridObjectToSpawnPrefab, GridManagerAccessor.GridManager.GetGridPosition(), Quaternion.identity);
  GridManagerAccessor.GridManager.EnterPlacementMode(objectToPlace);
  SimulationLoop.Instance.gridInScene.Add(@object);  // CreateItemBtn.cs L46/61/72
  ```
- `UI_TestPanelItemBTN.cs` also uses `GridManager.IsPlacingGridObject`, `GridManager.ObjectToPlace`, `GridManager.CancelPlacement(hideGrid:false)`, and a second Instantiate path (L194/205).
- `Assets\Scripts\ObjectMenuController.cs` re-enters placement mode for an existing object (`GridManagerAccessor.GridManager.EnterPlacementMode(currentOBJ)`).
- `Assets\GridPlacement\Runtime\Scripts\GridManager.cs` (namespace `Hypertonic.GridPlacement`) provides `EnterPlacementMode`, `DeleteObject`, `GetGridPosition`, `OnGridObjectDeleted` event, `IsPlacingGridObject`, `ObjectToPlace`, `CancelPlacement`.
- `Assets\GridPlacement\Runtime\Scripts\GridManagerAccessor.cs` — static accessor: `Dictionary<string,GridManager> _gridManagerDictionary`; `GridManager` static property returns selected/default; `RegisterGridManager`/`UnregisterGridManager`/`SetSelectedGridManager`. Accessed everywhere as `GridManagerAccessor.GridManager`.
- `Assets\Scripts\Item3D.cs` — component on placed objects: `public UI_TestPanelItemBTN itemUI;`, `public Item itemSelf;`, `public bool hasCreate=false;`. Implements IPointerUp/Down; fires `OnObjectSelected` event. NOTE: Item3D does NOT store position/rotation — those live on the Transform (and are managed by GridManager).

### 2. BaseValve + ValveName enum (`Assets\Scripts\Valve\BaseValve.cs`)
```csharp
public abstract class BaseValve : MonoBehaviour {
    public string valveName;
    public List<PneumaticPort> ports = new List<PneumaticPort>();
    protected virtual void Start() { if (SimulationLoop.Instance != null) SimulationLoop.Instance.allValves.Add(this); }
    public abstract void ProcessLogic();
    private void OnDestroy() { if (SimulationLoop.Instance != null) SimulationLoop.Instance.allValves.Remove(this); }
}
```
- **ValveName enum** (43 values, `[System.Serializable]`): 单电控二位三通电磁阀_常开/常闭, 单向节流阀, 滚轮式..., 快速排气节流阀, 气动二联件, 气动手滑阀, 气动双压阀, 气动梭阀, 气动延时阀_常开/常闭, 手动三位四通换向阀_O型, 双电控二位五通电磁阀, 双电控三位五通电磁阀_O型/Y型, 双气控..., 双作用单杆气缸, 单向压力顺序阀, 快速排气阀, 手动二位四通换向阀, 真空发生器, 双杆双轴气缸, 双向摆动回转气缸, 双向气动马达, 单作用气缸, 按钮式..., 机械式..., **三通, 四通, 主气源, 开关1, 开关2, 开关3**.
- **ValveState enum**: Left=-1, Center=0, Right=1.
- Concrete subclasses in `Assets\Scripts\Valve\` (ManualValve32/34, SolenoidValve32/52, PilotValve52, ThrottleValve, TimeDelayValve, OrShuttleValve, AndGateValve, SingleActingCylinder, DoubleActingCylinder, DoubleActingRotate, VacuumGenerator, FR_Unit, MainSourceCon, quickCalve, RollerValve32/32_B, SequenceCheckValve, SinglePilotValve52, valve32Button, etc.).

### 3. linerendeler class (`Assets\Scripts\Bezier\linerendeler.cs`) — wires/pipes
```csharp
[RequireComponent(typeof(LineRenderer))]
public class linerendeler : MonoBehaviour {
    public Transform p0;            // endpoint A (port anchor)
    public Transform p2;            // endpoint B (port anchor)
    public Transform handle20, handle50, handle80;  // Catmull-Rom control handles
    private portandvalve _wirePortA, _wirePortB;    // cached endpoint data
    private PortBase _wireBaseA, _wireBaseB;        // cached endpoint refs (for unregister)
    private bool isConnectionRegistered = false;
    ...
    RegisterConnection()  -> SimulationLoop.Instance.RegisterWire(portA, portB);
    UnregisterConnection()-> SimulationLoop.Instance.UnregisterWire(_wireBaseA, _wireBaseB);
    OnDestroy()           -> UnregisterConnection(); portA.Disconnect(); portB.Disconnect();
}
```
- Renders a Catmull-Rom spline (resolution ~50) between p0 and p2. Selects line on click → `SimulationLoop.Instance.currentLine = this.gameObject`.
- **For save/load**: a wire = two PortBase endpoints (p0/p2 Transforms). The endpoint data is `_wirePortA`/`_wirePortB` (portandvalve = ValveName + PneumaticPortName), but the *instance identity* is only recoverable via the PortBase Transform/portandvalve pair.
- Wire creation is triggered via `TubeBuilderManager.Instance.StartBuildPneumaticTube()` / `StartBuildtinckwireTube()` / `StartBuildwireTube()` (called from TraniningPanel buttons).

### 4. PortBase class (`Assets\Scripts\Valve\PortBase.cs`)
```csharp
public class PortBase : MonoBehaviour {
    public portandvalve portandvalve;   // { PneumaticPortName port; ValveName valve; }
    public portChanel chanel;           // none/pneumatic/tinckElec/simplleElec
    public bool isOccupied = false;     // 是否已连线 (connected)
    public bool isStackable = false;
    public bool isMain;
    public bool debugOn = false;
    public NodeType nodetype;
    public DynamicNode circuitNode;     // electrical circuit node
    public virtual void Propagate(); public virtual void OnConnect(PortBase port);
    public virtual void AlwaysON(); public virtual void Disconnect() { isOccupied=false; /* reset circuitNode */ }
}
public enum portChanel { none=0, pneumatic, tinckElec, simplleElec }
public enum PneumaticPortName { X,Y,A,B,P,R,Z1,Z2,L,M,v0,v24,L1,L2,L3,N }
[System.Serializable] public class portandvalve { public PneumaticPortName port; public ValveName valve; }
```
- Subclass `PneumaticPort` (`Assets\Scripts\Valve\PneumaticPort.cs`) extends PortBase (adds state, exPressure, inExFlow, outExFlow, internalConnectTo, ReceiveExternalInfo/IntegrateAndOutput/ClearPressureState, PortType.main, PortState.Conduct, etc.) — used by all valves.

### 5. SimulationLoop class (`Assets\Scripts\Valve\SimulationLoop.cs`) — registries
```csharp
public static SimulationLoop Instance; public static event Action OnInstanceCreated;
public List<BaseValve> allValves = new List<BaseValve>();
public List<PortBase> mainSources = new List<PortBase>();
public List<GameObject> gridInScene = new List<GameObject>();   // placed components
public GameObject currentLine;
public PneumaticTrainingCase CurrentCase;
public CustomList<caseportData> currentPostsData = new CustomList<caseportData>();
public trainType currenttrainType; public int Score = 100;

private class WireEntry { public portandvalve portAData, portBData; public string keyA, keyB; }
private readonly List<WireEntry> _wireRegistry = new List<WireEntry>();
```
- **RegisterWire(PortBase portA, PortBase portB)**: extracts portandvalve from each, builds keys, adds WireEntry, calls `RebuildGroups()`.
- **UnregisterWire(PortBase portA, PortBase portB)**: `RemoveAll` matching (bidirectional key match), `RebuildGroups()`.
- **GetPortKey(PortBase)** = `"{valve}_{port}_{gameObject.GetInstanceID()}"` — ⚠️ instanceID is NOT stable across save/load sessions; a save system must replace this with a persistent valve ID.
- **RebuildGroups()**: union-find; merges wired pairs, then merges all ports on each T_JointValve whose ports are wired (handles T-joint cascades). Builds `currentPostsData` (List of caseportData, each = List<portandvalve> nodes), only groups with ≥2 nodes.
- **DeleteAllValves()**: DeleteAllLines() first, then for each `gridInScene`: ReturnItemUI(v), `GridManagerAccessor.GridManager.DeleteObject(v)`; gridInScene.Clear(); removes from allValves.
- **DeleteAllLines()**: `_wireRegistry.Clear(); RebuildGroups();` then FindObjectsByType<linerendeler> → Destroy each.
- **RegisterValve(BaseValve)**, **ReturnItemUI(GameObject)** (increments itemUI.itemnum, decrements chazhi, UpdateUIState).
- Update loop: ResetAllPorts → 20× iteration of { ProcessLogic() per valve → ReceiveExternalInfo() per port → IntegrateAndOutput() per port }.

### 6. PneumaticTrainingCase + TraniningPanel (`Assets\Scripts\UI\TrainingPanel\TraniningPanel.cs`)
```csharp
[System.Serializable] public class PneumaticTrainingCase {
    [JsonProperty("CaseNamber")] public int CaseNamber {get;set;}
    [JsonProperty("Casname")] public string Casname {get;set;}
