### 8. T_JointValve (`Assets\Scripts\Valve\T_JointValve.cs`) — 三通 (and 四通 via ValveName)
```csharp
public class T_JointValve : BaseValve {
    private PneumaticPort coreHub;
    protected override void Start() {
        base.Start();
        GameObject hubObj = new GameObject("T_CoreHub_Virtual"); hubObj.transform.SetParent(this.transform);
        coreHub = hubObj.AddComponent<PneumaticPort>(); coreHub.state = PortState.Conduct;
        foreach (var port in ports) { port.state = PortState.Conduct; port.internalConnectTo = coreHub; }  // all 3 faces → hub
    }
    public override void ProcessLogic() { /* aggregates max exPressure into coreHub, distributes flow (Min bottleneck) */ }
}
```
- Differs from BaseValve: purely topological splitter/merger with an internal virtual hub; all ports Conduct; no switching state. `coreHub` is auto-created in Start (re-creatable on load — no need to serialize). 四通 (4-way) is a ValveName value handled the same way.

### 9. Prefab / ScriptableObject patterns for valve definitions
- **No ScriptableObject** for valves. Valves are MonoBehaviours on prefabs.
- `Item` class (`Assets\Scripts\ItemManager.cs`, `[System.Serializable]`) is the catalog entry: `string itemName; int itemID; Sprite itemImage; GameObject prefab; Sprite describeTexture; float price; string model; [TextArea] string itemDescription;` — plain serializable class, configured in Inspector (not a SO).
- `ComponentItem`/`PneumaticComponentsData` (`[Serializable]`) mirror a JSON components catalog: `name, type, iconName, category, describeText, describeImageName, describeVideoName, prefabName, Specification`.
