### 10. Valve spawning + catalog/inventory
- **Inventory**: `ItemManager : SingletonMono2<ItemManager>` (`Assets\Scripts\ItemManager.cs`) — `Dictionary<Item,int> inventory`; `AddItem/RemoveItem/ClearItem/ClearAllItemData`; bag UI via `iconRig` + `ItemSprite_factory` (item+count+model). `itemListGet_scripts` (ItemListGet_ui) feeds component selection; `Cinfirm_Rreceipt()` moves selected items to inventory.
- **Spawn entry**: `CreateItemBtn.cs` and `UI_TestPanelItemBTN.cs` (Instantiate prefab → `GridManagerAccessor.GridManager.EnterPlacementMode` → `gridInScene.Add`). `UI_TestPanelItemBTN` is the per-component button (referenced by `Item3D.itemUI`); has `itemnum`/`chazhi` counters and `UpdateUIState`.
- **Wire spawning**: `TubeBuilderManager` (`Assets\Scripts\Bezier\TubeBuilderManager.cs`) — `StartBuildPneumaticTube/StartBuildtinckwireTube/StartBuildwireTube` create linerendeler wires between two clicked ports.
- **Deletion**: `SimulationLoop.DeleteAllValves/DeleteAllLines`, single-line delete sets `SimulationLoop.Instance.currentLine` then Destroy. `UIManager_qidong.cs` subscribes to `GridManagerAccessor.GridManager.OnGridObjectDeleted`.

### Save/Load Design Implications (key gaps to address)
- **Runtime state to serialize**: (a) each valve in `gridInScene`/`allValves` → prefab/ValveName type + Transform position+rotation + (rotation/grid cell from GridManager); (b) each wire in `_wireRegistry` → two endpoints identified by (valve instance, PneumaticPortName).
- **Stable ID problem**: `GetPortKey` uses `GetInstanceID()` which is NOT stable across sessions. A save system must assign each placed valve a persistent int/string ID (e.g. on Item3D or BaseValve) and key ports by `{valveId}_{PneumaticPortName}`.
- **Position source**: BaseValve has no position field — use `transform.position`/`transform.rotation`; verify GridManager can place at an exact world pos (it has `GetGridPosition()` + `EnterPlacementMode`; need a "place at saved position" path, currently only interactive placement exists).
- **T_JointValve coreHub**: auto-recreated in Start() — no serialization needed.
- **caseportData/portandvalve** are already `[Serializable]` and JSON-friendly (Newtonsoft available) — reusable as the wire serialization DTO. `currentPostsData` is derived (rebuilt by RebuildGroups) so only `_wireRegistry`-equivalent endpoint pairs need saving.
- **Load order**: instantiate valves & assign IDs → register in allValves/gridInScene → recreate wires (Instantiate linerendeler, set p0/p2 to matching port Transforms, call RegisterWire) → RebuildGroups runs automatically.

Next steps:
Implement a save/load system: (1) Add a persistent valve ID field (e.g. on Item3D or a new SaveableValve component) generated at spawn time in CreateItemBtn/UI_TestPanelItemBTN. (2) Build a SaveData DTO ([Serializable]) holding List<ValveSaveData{valveId, valveName/ValveName, pos, rot}> and List<WireSaveData{valveIdA, portA(PneumaticPortName), valveIdB, portB}>. (3) On save, iterate SimulationLoop.gridInScene/allValves + _wireRegistry (expose a getter or add SaveWires()). (4) On load, clear via DeleteAllValves, instantiate prefabs by ValveName (map ValveName→Item.prefab via ItemManager inventory or a catalog), place at saved pos/rot (extend GridManager usage or set Transform directly), assign IDs, then recreate linerendeler wires between matching ports and call RegisterWire. (5) Use Newtonsoft.Json (already in project) to write/read to Application.persistentDataPath. Verify GridManager supports exact-position placement or bypass it for loaded objects.
